      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-3,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=11,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{1}{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{1}{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{4}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-3+11) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
